From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:59:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] pro1xkbd: scan held keys every 30 ms

The AW9523B interrupts on input changes, not on the release of a held
key, so the matrix is scanned while a key is down: every 30 ms instead
of 15 still catches the shortest presses with half the I2C traffic and
wake-ups.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/dev/iicbus/pro1x_kbd.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/iicbus/pro1x_kbd.c b/sys/dev/iicbus/pro1x_kbd.c
index 687efbc32..c48f0f21f 100644
--- a/sys/dev/iicbus/pro1x_kbd.c
+++ b/sys/dev/iicbus/pro1x_kbd.c
@@ -59,7 +59,12 @@
 #define	AW_SOFT_RESET	0x7f
 
 #define	NLINES		8
-#define	POLL_MS		15
+/*
+ * While a key is down the matrix is scanned every POLL_MS (the AW9523B
+ * only interrupts on changes of its inputs, not on release of a held
+ * key): 30 ms still catches the shortest presses and halves the scans
+ */
+#define	POLL_MS		30
 #define	SCAN_RETRIES	10
 #define	SETTLE_US	20
 
